Third-party notices for taraba-generated packages
================================================

The taraba JavaScript runtime and generated binding support are MIT licensed;
see LICENSE.taraba. The application's own license is set in package.json.

If the Wasm includes taraba-allocator, its covered portions are MPL-2.0,
including modifications derived from wee_alloc_bw / wee_alloc. The MPL source
rights are independent of the application's license. See LICENSE.taraba-allocator
and UPSTREAM.taraba-allocator.json for the license and upstream provenance.

The source of unmodified taraba-allocator 0.1.0 is available as
a Cargo source archive, including its license, provenance and build files:
https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/taraba-allocator/0.1.0/download
Project: https://github.com/mizchi/taraba

The allocator uses memory_units 0.4.0 (MPL-2.0), by Nick Fitzgerald and Sergey
Pepyakin. Its source, including its MPL license, is available at:
https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/memory_units/0.4.0/download
Project: https://github.com/pepyakin/memory_units

These notices are included for all builds, even if optimization removes the
allocator or a different allocator is selected. They describe the version
bundled with this CLI's scaffolds, not an inspection of arbitrary input Wasm.
If you use another version or modified covered source (including path/patch
dependencies), update the source locations to the exact version/modifications
you distribute and make that source available under MPL-2.0. Review licenses
of other application dependencies separately. Keep applicable notices and source
access information available when redistributing the Wasm outside this package.
